---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Eliminating Lecture Hall Overlaps in Higher Education"
  description="Practical guide to preventing classroom and lecture hall collision in Cameroonian universities."
  lang="en"
  alternateUrlFr="/fr/blog/1/"
  alternateUrlEn="/en/blog/1/"
>
  <article class="py-20 bg-slate-50 text-slate-900">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-md">
      <a href="/en/blog/" class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-600 hover:underline mb-6 block">← Back to articles</a>
      <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block mb-2">October 5, 2026 • 4 min read</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-6">Eliminating Lecture Hall Overlaps in Cameroonian Higher Education</h1>
      
      <div class="prose prose-slate text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-slate-700">
        <p>In many higher education institutions across Cameroon, classroom management still relies on physical notice boards or uncoordinated Excel files. The result? Lecturers and hundreds of students arriving simultaneously at the same lecture hall.</p>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-6 mb-2">The Solution: Real-Time Collision Algorithms</h2>
        <p>Pineapple OS introduces automated validation during timetable creation. The moment a slot is assigned to a course or lecturer, the hall is locked for that timeframe.</p>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mt-6 mb-2">The Decisive Role of Class Delegates</h2>
        <p>When a lecturer finishes early, class delegates report real-time room availability via the app, making the hall instantly available for catch-up sessions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
